Your letter 035, taken.
1. LK1: the build takes the designer's look (publishing/lab-look.css after book.css), the book and the sample; the book is 254 pages in it, the sample 13. The prompt line under the title is off while NS1 is open. Security has the one sample change since its clearance (page 5's 182, the researcher's fix).
2. The ink, from KDP's own pages (KDP.md has the table and the sources): printing cost depends on ink and page count only; KDP prices nothing per image, so his reading holds within an ink. At 255 pages, 6 x 9: black $4.06 a copy; standard colour $7.50; premium colour $17.58. The royalty is 60% of the list price less printing (from $9.99; 50% below). At $19.99 a copy earns about $7.93 in black, about $4.49 in standard colour, and nothing in premium colour, which cannot be sold below about $29.29. The PDF and EPUB print nothing; the EPUB's delivery cost at 70% grows with heavier images ($0.15 a MB).
For him: the ink for the paperback, as a choice: black (the pictures in grey), standard colour (the look as designed, about $3.44 more a copy), or premium.

